F632 [*] Use `==` to compare constant literals
 --> F632_basedpython.by:4:11
  |
2 | # parser flattens to the same operator. only the identity spellings compare identity
3 | def identity(x: object) -> None:
4 |     print(1 === 1)  # F632
  |           ^^^^^^^
5 |     print(x !== "a")  # F632
  |
help: Replace `===` with `==`
  |
3 | def identity(x: object) -> None:
  -     print(1 === 1)  # F632
4 +     print(1 == 1)  # F632
5 |     print(x !== "a")  # F632
